#
# initramfs-tools RUNTIME hook, init-premount: photograph whoever is at the
# keyboard BEFORE the LUKS passphrase prompt. Equivalent of dracut's
# pre-trigger hook.
#
# Stage matters: cryptsetup runs from local-top, and init-premount is the last
# stage that finishes before it. Putting this in local-top instead would race
# the passphrase prompt, and a photo taken after the machine is unlocked
# answers a different question.
#
# The work is backgrounded by the script itself and never blocks boot: a photo
# needs no ciphertext, so nothing here is allowed to delay the prompt.

PREREQ=""
prereqs() { echo "$PREREQ"; }
case "$1" in
    prereqs) prereqs; exit 0 ;;
esac

[ -x /usr/libexec/sysentinel/sysentinel-precrypt.sh ] || exit 0
/usr/libexec/sysentinel/sysentinel-precrypt.sh || true

exit 0
